# Messages the file mailer writes in development. Correspondence, and not
# something to commit.
#
# Named by its full path rather than as "mail/", which is what it said, and
# which cost this repository its entire mail module. An unanchored pattern
# matches a directory of that name at any depth, git on Windows is configured
# case-insensitively, and so "mail/" quietly swallowed
# src/JiranisokoTech.Application/Mail and src/JiranisokoTech.Infrastructure/Mail
# as well. Eleven source files were written, built, tested and committed
# against — and none of them was ever in a commit. Nothing said so: the working
# tree compiled, the suite was green, and `git status` reported clean, because
# as far as git was concerned there was nothing there. It surfaces only in a
# fresh clone, as four compiler errors about a namespace that does not exist.
/src/JiranisokoTech.Web/mail/

# Candidate CVs written by the file store. Documents belonging to people
# outside this firm, and not something to commit.
/src/JiranisokoTech.Web/cvs/

# Worktrees the agent tooling creates. Not part of the project.
.claude/worktrees/
